      "reason": "The finding correctly uses airport_dropoffs_per_hour as a normalized metric. Both total trips and airport_dropoffs_per_hour are higher on the rainy day (105.4 vs 83.5). The data cleanly refutes the claim that rain shifted demand away from airport trips or toward nearer zones.",
      "revision_request": null
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "verdict": "accept",
      "reason": "The finding correctly compares airport_trips_per_hour across the two days. Airport trips and airport_trips_per_hour are both higher on the rainy day (419.5 vs 382.7). The data cleanly refutes the claim that rain disproportionately reduced airport-related trips.",
      "revision_request": null
    }
  ],
